{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478020-how-do-you-pronounce-siberakh","id":1478020,"title":"How do you pronounce Siberakh?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-04T16:41:53-07:00","id":1478020,"title":"How do you pronounce Siberakh?","content":"Hopefully a simple question. So far they're involved in a campaign I'm working on, all while trying to read sources, and haven't gotten to Rage Across Russia yet. If you want to throw in any extra thoughts on them, that would be cool.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T16:56:18-07:00","id":1478021,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming the question is on the ending (Siber- should be like Siberia)?<br /> <br /> Given the area in question, I assume the kh here is the Cyrillic X, which is based on the Greek X, or chi, which is a hard c. For people not used to it, rhyming with &quot;ack&quot; (like back) is close enough. For going for a bit more detail you'd want to be a bit closer to the Scottish &quot;loch&quot;, &quot;bock&quot; as a style of beer, or &quot;Bach&quot; like the composer. IME the hardest part of getting the sound right for people unfamiliar with it is that they're not used to it ending a word and have an easier time practicing it with a vowel first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T17:17:33-07:00","id":1478022,"title":"","content":"My Russian teacher described the cyrillic x as the &quot;laughing letter&quot;. XA XA XA XA!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T18:40:28-07:00","id":1478028,"title":"","content":"IIRC in Russian it's different if there's a vowel after it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T00:36:19-07:00","id":1478036,"title":"","content":"Question on the ending too, does \u201ckh\u201d mean \u201cpeople\u201d like Japan-Japanese?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T01:24:15-07:00","id":1478039,"title":"","content":"Most likely not? At least it doesn't in any of the extant languages that would make sense for the area. However their are a very large number of them, so etymology of the names of places and peoples in central and northern Asia can be very contested. There's no pattern of it in either the various local names people call themselves, or the spread of it from a dominant language from the empires that have controlled the area (ex: you don't seen peoples conquered by the Mongols all ending up with &quot;-kh&quot; at the end of their demonyms; demonym is the word you're looking for for &quot;people&quot; here btw).<br /> <br /> While most of the original WoD names can be sussed out on where the authors got them from, I'm pretty sure this one's going to be a mystery without input from the creatives involved or someone that talked to them about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T17:58:16-07:00","id":1478104,"title":"","content":"A quick etymology check on Wiktionary shows that the -ir is the &quot;people of&quot; particle, and the reference to Sibe means &quot;scattered around&quot;, as with a river's delta deposits of soil. A similar sounding Russian word to Siberakh, sibirjak, means &quot;a resident of Siberia&quot;, one of several ways of relating this residence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T03:30:54-07:00","id":1485181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478020-how-do-you-pronounce-siberakh?p=1478104#post1478104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick etymology check on Wiktionary shows that the -ir is the &quot;people of&quot; particle, and the reference to Sibe means &quot;scattered around&quot;, as with a river's delta deposits of soil. A similar sounding Russian word to Siberakh, sibirjak, means &quot;a resident of Siberia&quot;, one of several ways of relating this residence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're close to it! The first half, sibirjak, is indeed meant to refer to those indigenous to siberia, but the second half is a slightly more sinister polish word, a slang, syrbiak. It's the casual reference for a political prisoner that has been exiled to die in siberia. Source is quoted from Heart of the Forest, which while isn't the total picture of what W5 will be, has been cited as an accurate depiction. Siberakh identify with both of the above definitions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T07:40:30-07:00","id":1485188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478020-how-do-you-pronounce-siberakh?p=1485181#post1485181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're close to it! The first half, sibirjak, is indeed meant to refer to those indigenous to siberia, but the second half is a slightly more sinister polish word, a slang, syrbiak. It's the casual reference for a political prisoner that has been exiled to die in siberia. Source is quoted from Heart of the Forest, which while isn't the total picture of what W5 will be, has been cited as an accurate depiction. Siberakh identify with both of the above definitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irony, that - if my grandfather hadn't been tormented to hell and back for learning Polish before English in the early 20th century US, I could potentially have known that!<br /> <br /> (He put down a mandate that my mother and her siblings not learn Polish at all. What I have is a terribly broken remnant of what my mother picked up from her grandparents.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T11:57:51-07:00","id":1485201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478020-how-do-you-pronounce-siberakh?p=1485188#post1485188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Irony, that - if my grandfather hadn't been tormented to hell and back for learning Polish before English in the early 20th century US, I could potentially have known that!<br /> <br /> (He put down a mandate that my mother and her siblings not learn Polish at all. What I have is a terribly broken remnant of what my mother picked up from her grandparents.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough that sentiment is intended to be a common one in werewolf backgrounds, as it's a common theme among US citizens. My great grandpa also forbade polish being spoken in the household or in public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}